Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.43,0:00:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,As we follow the path a light flickers In our story this\Nrepresents noise Quantum systems
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.42,0:00:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,interact with their surroundings and imperfect\Noperations can change the state we want to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.25,0:00:15.91,Default,,0,0,0,,preserve There are bit errors phase errors and other\Nkinds of disturbance Engineers
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.92,0:00:21.07,Default,,0,0,0,,improve isolation calibrate controls and develop ways to\Ndetect and correct errors An
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.08,0:00:25.68,Default,,0,0,0,,ideal simulator helps us understand the circuit's\Nintended behavior A noise model can
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.69,0:00:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,explore some imperfections Neither kind of test should\Nbe confused with a result measured
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.23,0:00:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,on a physical computer We must always say where the\Nexperiment was run and which
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.31,0:00:35.29,Default,,0,0,0,,assumptions we used